3.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: The positive exemplars dad,dab,gut,low,cat are all 3-letter C V C and contain no e,m,p,r. The negative exemplars ear,cop,ego,mom,ate all contain at least one of e,m,p,r and/or break C V C. The majority reading in rounds 0-1 is therefore “C V C and e,m,p,r-free”, effectively the ten-letter alphabet {a,b,c,d,g,l,o,t,u,w} with middle typically {a,u,o} and final typically {b,d,t,w}.

On that reading:
* leg = l e g contains e
* dam = d a m contains m, final m ∉ {b,d,t,w}
* rat = r a t contains r, first r ∉ {c,d,g,l}
* car = c a r contains r, final r ∉ {b,d,t,w}
are all non-pattern, the same type as ear/cop/ego/mom/ate. 
* bin = b i n is C V C and e,m,p,r-free. It is the only option that is of the same family as dad/dab/gut/low/cat under the e,m,p,r-free C V C description.

Colleagues 1,2,3,4,5,6,8,7 consistently name A–D as canonical non-followers, with A. leg repeatedly cited as the textbook e-containing non-member, dam as the m-containing analogue of mom, rat/car as the r-containing analogues of ear. Colleague10 explicitly votes E. bin as the odd-one-out / unique pattern follower.

Unresolved tension: Colleague 9 and the stricter refinement used by some in round 1 impose middle ∈ {a,u,o} and final ∈ {d,b,t,w}. Under that stricter inventory bin fails on middle i and final n, leg fails on e/g, dam fails on final m, car fails on final r, and rat is the only option that satisfies middle a / final t albeit with first r outside the positive first-letter set {c,d,g,l}. This strict inventory vs the looser e,m,p,r-free C V C split is still open, and the question wording “which of the words does not follow the pattern?” is ambiguous between asking for a canonical non-member among A–D, e.g. A. leg, and asking for the unique option that does follow the pattern, i.e. E. bin, which is the odd-one-out in the list. Current weight of evidence favors the e,m,p,r-free C V C majority description, with A–D all non-pattern and E. bin the unique pattern follower; A. leg remains the most cited single non-pattern example.

